 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Division by $\sqrt{D}$ requires $D > 0$.
-*   **Boundaries:** Coordinate normalization assumes $W > 1$ and $H > 1$ to avoid division by zero.
-*   **Coordinate Scaling:** Off-by-one errors can occur if `coords` are not properly normalized to $[-1, 1]$ before division by $2^i$.
-*   **Tensor Layout:** The `einsum` string `'aijk,aijh->ajkh'` assumes a specific dimension ordering; mismatched input layouts will produce incorrect correlation shapes.
